#: ../../../connect_to_workbook.md:1
msgid "Connect to a Book"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../connect_to_workbook.md:3
msgid "Python to Excel"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../connect_to_workbook.md:5
msgid ""
"The easiest way to connect to a book is offered by `xw.Book`: it looks for "
"the book in all app instances and returns an error, should the same book be "
"open in multiple instances. To connect to a book in the active app instance, "
"use `xw.books` and to refer to a specific app, use:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../connect_to_workbook.md:14
msgid ""
"Note that you usually should use `App` as a context manager as this will "
"make sure that the Excel instance is closed and cleaned up again properly:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../connect_to_workbook.md:0
msgid "xw.Book"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../connect_to_workbook.md:0
msgid "xw.books"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../connect_to_workbook.md:0
msgid "New book"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../connect_to_workbook.md:0
msgid "`xw.Book()`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../connect_to_workbook.md:0
msgid "`xw.books.add()`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../connect_to_workbook.md:0
msgid "Unsaved book"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../connect_to_workbook.md:0
msgid "`xw.Book('Book1')`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../connect_to_workbook.md:0
msgid "`xw.books['Book1']`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../connect_to_workbook.md:0
msgid "Book by (full)name"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../connect_to_workbook.md:0
msgid "`xw.Book(r'C:/path/to/file.xlsx')`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../connect_to_workbook.md:0
msgid "`xw.books.open(r'C:/path/to/file.xlsx')`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../connect_to_workbook.md:28
msgid ""
"When specifying file paths on Windows, you should either use raw strings by "
"putting an `r` in front of the string or use double back-slashes like so: `C:"
"\\\\path\\\\to\\\\file.xlsx`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../connect_to_workbook.md:32
msgid "Excel to Python (RunPython)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../connect_to_workbook.md:34
msgid ""
"To reference the calling book when using `RunPython` in VBA, use `xw.Book."
"caller()`, see [Call Python with \"RunPython\"](vba.md#call-python-with-"
"runpython). Check out the section about [Debugging](debugging.md#debugging) "
"to see how you can call a script from both sides, Python and Excel, without "
"the need to constantly change between `xw.Book.caller()` and one of the "
"methods explained above."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../connect_to_workbook.md:39
msgid "User Defined Functions (UDFs)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../connect_to_workbook.md:41
msgid ""
"Unlike `RunPython`, UDFs don't need a call to `xw.Book.caller()`, see [User "
"Defined Functions (UDFs)](udfs.md#user-defined-functions-udfs). You'll "
"usually use the `caller` argument which returns the xlwings range object "
"from where you call the function."
msgstr ""
